      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 44-year-old woman was referred to physical therapy by a podiatrist for \"iliotibial band syndrome.\" No imaging had been done, and she denied all constitutional symptoms, but reported having breast cancer 5 years earlier. Following an increase in pain, radiographs and magnetic resonance imaging were performed, and biopsy confirmed a metastatic breast cancer tumor. J Orthop Sports Phys Ther 2016;46(5):400. doi:10.2519/jospt.2016.0407."},
